# ===========================================================================
# search/.env.example - the SEARCH plane's own environment
# (stack-layers L.2 / D10 / D17, 2026-09-19)
# ===========================================================================
# Private Search Gateway: privacy-first web search over Mullvad (tor retired
# 2026-08-21).
# Guide: ../documentation-plans-ai-stack/implementation-guide/web-search/guide-Private-Search-Gateway.md
#
# Copy to `search/.env` and fill in. Compose loads it NATIVELY: passing
# `-f search/docker-compose.yml` makes `search/` the PROJECT DIRECTORY, and
# compose reads the `.env` sitting there. No `--env-file` flag, from any
# working directory - which is why the guard in the compose file names THIS
# file.
#
# THE SPLIT RULE (D10): a variable lives in the .env of the plane whose service
# reads it. A value two planes read is DECLARED IN EACH - the plane files are
# independent and compose cannot reference one from another. Open WebUI's side
# of the web-search wiring (ENABLE_WEB_SEARCH / WEB_SEARCH_ENGINE /
# SEARXNG_QUERY_URL) is therefore in frontend/.env, not here: those three are
# read by the openwebui container, not by anything on this plane.
#
# WHAT IS IN HERE: exactly the variables `search/docker-compose.yml`
# interpolates. This plane declares NO compose profiles, so there is no
# COMPOSE_PROFILES line (D17).
#
# Migrating an existing deployment: documentation/runbooks/env-split-migration.md.

# --- REQUIRED - generate long random strings (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`) ---
# GATEWAY_API_KEY is the gateway's one REQUIRED Settings field
# (search/gateway/src/gateway/config.py:17-21 - `Field(...)`), and the container
# crash-loops on 'GATEWAY_API_KEY Field required' without it.
GATEWAY_API_KEY=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
SEARXNG_SECRET_KEY=change-me-to-another-long-random-string

# --- Mullvad WireGuard (ALL search-plane egress) -----------------------------
# MULLVAD_WG_PRIVATE_KEY carries a ${...:?} fail-loud guard in
# search/docker-compose.yml, and the guard rejects EMPTY - hence the
# placeholder rather than a blank line.
# NOTE: MULLVAD_WG_ADDRESSES must be IPv4-only unless the Docker host has IPv6
# (gluetun rejects v6 addrs).
MULLVAD_WG_PRIVATE_KEY=change-me-real-wg-private-key
MULLVAD_WG_ADDRESSES=
MULLVAD_COUNTRIES=Netherlands

# Docker's default subnet pool; lets the LAN-side (search-net) reach gluetun's
# HTTP proxy through the kill-switch firewall.
SEARCH_NET_SUBNET=172.16.0.0/12

# --- Pinned images (reproducible privacy infra) ------------------------------
# Pinned 2026-09-11 (research-trust). The engine policy in
# search/searxng/settings.yml only works on this build or newer; on the
# 2026-05-17 image only yandex answers. Bump deliberately, with a
# re-measurement, never by floating :latest.
SEARXNG_IMAGE=searxng/searxng:2026.9.11-61d660276
SEARCH_REDIS_IMAGE=redis:7-alpine
VPN_IMAGE=qmcgaw/gluetun:latest

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT WIRED - gateway tunables that setting here would NOT change
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The seven names below are real pydantic Settings fields in
# search/gateway/src/gateway/config.py (:28-40), but NOTHING puts them into the
# gateway container today: `env_file: ../.env` was removed from that service on
# 2026-08-28 and its `environment:` block names only GATEWAY_API_KEY,
# SEARXNG_URL and REDIS_URL (search/docker-compose.yml:154-161). They sat in the
# root .env.example carrying their defaults, which reads like a knob and is not
# one - so they are listed here as PROSE, with the code default beside each,
# rather than silently dropped or silently pretended-live.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT `#NAME=value` lines: a commented-out assignment invites
# somebody to uncomment it, and uncommenting one of these would change nothing
# while looking like it had. There is nothing here to uncomment.
#
# To make one genuinely adjustable: add it to that `environment:` block as
# `- NAME=${NAME:-<default>}`, AND add a real assignment line here, in the same
# change.
#   CACHE_TTL_SECONDS          default 900
#   PROVIDER_PRIORITY          default searxng
#   REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS    default 20
#   CIRCUIT_FAILURE_THRESHOLD  default 3
#   CIRCUIT_COOLDOWN_SECONDS   default 120
#   LOG_LEVEL                  default INFO
#   LOG_QUERIES                default false  (PRIVACY: keep false; true logs
#                                              only a sha256 of the query)
